            <ArticleTitle>Chronic scrotal and inguinal pain after orchidopexy in a 13-year-old boy, treated by pulsed radiofrequency of the dorsal ganglia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e155-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpurol.2013.03.018</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1477-5131(13)00105-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic scrotal pain can be a difficult clinical entity to treat. Many different treatment options have been proposed. We describe the case of a young boy with chronic scrotal and inguinal pain on the right side, following two orchidopexies. After many therapies had failed, we treated the dorsal root ganglia of thoracic 12, lumbar 1 and lumbar 2 with pulsed radiofrequency, finally resulting in alleviation of his pain.</AbstractText>
